{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/512770-help-starting-a-new-group","id":512770,"title":"help: starting a new group","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-13T03:24:57-07:00","id":512770,"title":"help: starting a new group","content":"Hello, I'm starting a new werewolf game in a month or so, and I've never ran this splat before, (although I'm not totally unfamiliar) and I need some advice And have some questions. <br /> <br /> If there is an active pack in a given area, and the new PCs are integrated into it, but largely go on hunts only as the PCs, would they also be considered a pack? Basically would the PCs be a pack within a pack?<br /> <br /> I currently don't have the second edition book, however I mechanically understand W:TF 1st. Any mechanical difference between 1st and 2nd wolves? Are they more powerful? Do they heal faster/easier? Do they have access to agg damage easier? Can they regain essence easier?<br /> <br /> thanks all. I want to be best prepared so I can craft a rewarding experience for my players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1898-wadesauce","name":"wadesauce","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1898_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T10:08:35-07:00","id":513037,"title":"","content":"Packs are now much larger, typically being a human group built around Wolf-Blooded who are in the know and a core group of werewolves who engage in the activities of the Hunt.<br /> <br /> Werewolf regeneration starts at a point of bashing per turn and upgrades that healing to lethal damage with a point of Essence as before, but now rising Primal Urge increases the rate starting at PU4; also, aggravated damage is now restored on the 1e Quick Healer timer of one point per four days.<br /> <br /> Gauru form now automatically heals all bashing and lethal damage every turn and a lot of the Strength and Rage Gifts kick in automatically and for free while you're in Death Rage. All the forms have some particular innate ability like Hishu's carried-over-but-changed-from-1e unremarkability or Urshul's ability to make its first hit in a scene cause a Tilt representing a physical impairment like Arm Wrack or Knocked Down.<br /> <br /> The Sacred Hunt rite is now a two-dot rite that any starting werewolf can spend their free two dots of rites on, one of the new Lunacy Conditions increases the amount of Essence you can gain from eating a person's flesh, and fetishes can now be destroyed to consume their binding Essence. Werewolf metabolism now gradually shifts to be more spiritlike with higher PU as a take on the old Essence bleed drawback, first changing to draw sustenance only from raw meat, then only from the meat of carnivores, then only from Essence; Essence bleed is instead the result of spending too long not being on the Sacred Hunt, with &quot;too long&quot; shortening as Primal Urge rises.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}